-- #822: the graded-head lookup is keyed by the type-parameter NAME, because a
-- `TyVar h` spine head carries no interface context.  Two graded interfaces that
-- spell their head the same way with DIFFERENT slot kinds (`f e a` vs `f a e`)
-- therefore POISON that name, and both degrade to the pre-#822 opaque abstract
-- head — i.e. both are REJECTED by T-EFFECT-ARG-UNCOVERED rather than one of them
-- silently adopting the other's kinds.  Loud degradation is the point: this pins
-- that the ambiguity can never be resolved by accident of declaration order.
interface GA f where
  ga : f e a -> (a -> <e> f e b) -> f e b

interface GB f where
  gb : f a e -> (a -> <e> f a e) -> f a e
